' WatchStateBuffer — the player → MainScene watch-state mailbox.
'
' PlayerScreen publishes each position update here (memory-only) as well as
' through its own node field, so MainScene can still read the last packet after
' the player node is torn down — its async field observer races the pop that
' releases the component (and the video node it holds). Reading from this shared
' instance has no node-lifetime dependency.
'
' A last-value stash with no clearing: MainScene dedups repeated updates by
' videoId + position, so "latest" is all it needs. Constructed once under
' MainScene scope and shipped through the stores map (like TimeUtil and
' WatchedCodec), never built inside a method.
class WatchStateBuffer
    sub new()
        m.packet = invalid
    end sub

    ' Keep the newest packet. invalid publishes are ignored.
    sub Record(packet as dynamic)
        if packet = invalid then return
        m.packet = packet
    end sub

    ' The most recent packet, invalid before the first Record.
    function Latest() as dynamic
        return m.packet
    end function
end class